R-PB8 R-E7 R-P3 R-RC4 R-EC1 R-OUT2 (gap test of the design change of 2026-10-26, C7 of docs/slices/DESIGN-GAPS-2026-10-26.md): the exit code of `tln probe` for the two results that `probe/pc1-targets` does not show. `tln probe` exits 0 when it printed a fact (R-PB8, R-E7), and exit 1 only when there is no fact to print. The project, the packages, the compiler (`nightly-2026-10-14-38a3029` on PATH, nothing to download) and the config are those of `probe/pc1-targets`. 2 runs, each with one unit check.
Run 1: the unit check of acme/json 2.1.0 ends with SIGSEGV (`signal:11`). A crash is a fact (R-RC4, R-P3): the line `unit check ...: crash` is printed, the fact is written with `existing=replace`, exit 0.
Run 2: the unit check of the platform acme/pf 0.1.0 ends with SIGKILL (`signal:9`, as the OOM killer). A signal from outside gives no fact (R-P3): no fact is written, nothing is printed on stdout, exit 1 (kind `internal`, R-EC1): `the unit check of ... gave no result: signal 9. Run the command again.` The text of the failure is the text of the code (`ProbeUnit`, R-OUT2: not a design text).
The fail, the hang and the pass (exit 0) are in `probe/pc1-targets` runs 1 to 3. The case of a `--range` with no pass and a fact for each release (exit 0) is a row of the L0 test of `ProbeCmd.stop` (`ProbecmdTest`, row "no pass and a fact for each release").
